Stage 3 of the mechanics proposal: kinds and overtime together, then Dot khach, then tuning.
Everything below is the output of tools/sim, kept as printed. Newest and final is PART 4; read that first.

Final constants, all in src/game/rules.ts:
  FIRST_WAVE 3, MAX_WAVE 6, WAVE_GROWTH_DAYS 5 (group 3 on days 1-5, 4 on 6-10, 5 on 11-15, 6 from 16)
  LULL 6-10 s, WAVE_GAP 1.2-2.2 s
  LINE_MS 35 s                 (brief's start: about 25 s)
  DAY_PATIENCE_FLOOR_MS 65 s   (was a literal 60 s in levels.ts)
  OVERTIME_PATIENCE 0.7        (brief's start: 0.8)
  OVERTIME_BONUS_PER_ROUND 0.1 (brief's start: 0.15)
  OVERTIME_BURN_KEEPS 0.5      (unmoved: decision 2)
  Kind rules and the two floors under them: unmoved. A round's group: config.waveSize, as the brief says.

Which part was run on what:
  PART 1  before any wave code, on the brief's starting overtime constants, n=300.
  PART 2  sweeps, in the order they were run. These predate two fixes and two later constants, so read them
          for direction and not for level: the wave and overtime sweeps ran with a bug that gave the day's
          first group a quiet of its own, and on a day floor of 60 s; OVERTIME_GROUP_EXTRA existed for them,
          was shown to add nothing, and is gone. The day-floor sweep ran on the 30 s line.
  PART 3  the line-wait sweep, on the final day floor, which is what chose 35 s.
  PART 4  the final pass on the final constants, n=300, then the sensitivity sweep around them, n=120.
  PART 5  the day floor and the line wait again on the bot that PART 4 uses, which is what kept 65 s and 35 s.

PARTS 1 TO 3 ran on a bot that read every customer's exact deadline from any page. PARTS 4 AND 5 ran on the
bot that decides from what is on screen (tools/sim/README.md), so compare them for direction only. PART 4's
section F is new with that change.


################ PART 1. KINDS AND OVERTIME TOGETHER, BEFORE WAVES

